epared by the Seabreeze Town Council project team, close-out report, June 2021.", "Shared with Harbourline Town Council for reference.", "", "Project summary: 7,200 m2 hub, 1991 building. Budget S$12.8M, final cost S$14.1M.", "Planned 18 months, actual 23 months. Hub kept open throughout.", "", "L01 Keeping the hub open", "    Keeping all floors open added about 3 months and S$0.6M (temporary works,", "    night shifts, resequencing). Residents later said a short, well-announced", "    closure would have been preferable to 18 months of partial disruption.", "    Recommendation: agree closures with the sponsor before contract award.", "", "L02 Noise", "    31 formal noise complaints, 22 of them in months 4–7 during hacking works.", "    Complaints fell once a weekly works notice was posted at lift lobbies.", "", "L03 Hazardous materials", "    Asbestos was found in ceiling boards in month 3 despite a desk study saying none", "    was expected. Removal added 5 weeks. Recommendation: commission an intrusive", "    hazardous-materials survey for any pre-2000 building before tender.", "", "L04 Childcare licensing", "    The childcare operator needed about 7 months between floor handover and first", "    intake (fit-out, inspections, licence). The project had allowed 3.", "", "L05 Late operator appointment", "    The senior activity centre operator was appointed in month 14, after the layout", "    was fixed. Two rooms had to be reconfigured at a cost of S$85,000.", "", "L06 Consultation", "    The online survey drew 80% of responses, mostly from residents under 45.", "    Seniors, the main users of two of the new facilities, were under-represented.", "    A second round with door-to-door and multilingual paper forms changed the", "    priority order of three features.", "", "L07 Reporting", "    Weekly written status reports to the committee were rarely read in full.", "    From month 9 the team switched to a one-page exception report: what changed,", "    what is late, what needs a decision. Committee time on decisions doubled.", "", "L08 Grant claims", "    One grant tranche was delayed 4 months because a condition (signed operator", "    agreements) had been missed in the project schedule. Recommendation: put every", "    grant condition into the schedule as a milestone with an owner."]}, {"id": "07_Grant_milestone_tranche_schedule.txt", "lines": ["NEIGHBOURHOOD RENEWAL FUND (NRF) — LETTER OF GRANT CONDITIONS (EXTRACT)", "Recipient: Harbourline Town Council", "Project: Harbourline Community Hub Refurbishment", "Reference: NRF/2026/HCH-017 · Issued 19 January 2027", "", "1. GRANT AMOUNT", "   1.1 The grant is 60% of eligible project cost.", "   1.2 Eligible project cost is capped at S$17.0 million. Maximum grant S$10.2 million.", "   1.3 Ineligible items include: refurbishment of commercial premises (including food", "       courts and leased retail), and landscaping or rooftop amenity not forming part", "       of a social service facility.", "   1.4 Cost increases above the cap are borne by the recipient.", "", "2. TRANCHES", "   | Tranche | Share of grant | Release condition                                                    |", "   |---------|----------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|", "   | T1      | 20%            | Contract award and submission of baseline programme                  |", "   | T2      | 30%            | Completion of structural and M&E rough-in, AND signed operator        |", "   |         |                | agreements for ALL social service spaces in the facility             |", "   | T3      | 30%            | Temporary Occupation Permit (TOP) for the whole facility              |", "   | T4      | 20%            | Six months of operation and submission of a utilisation report        |", "", "3. REPORTING", "   3.1 A monthly progress report is due by the 10th working day of each month.", "   3.2 It must state: progress against the baseline programme, expenditure to date", "       against eligible cost, status of each tranche condition, and top five risks.", "   3.3 Two consecutive late or incomplete reports may suspend the next tranche.", "", "4. CHANGES", "   4.1 Any change to the scope of social service facilities (childcare, active ageing,", "       accessibility works) requires the Fund's prior written approval.", "   4.2 Completion later than 31 December 2028 requires the Fund's prior approval.", "", "5. ACCESSIBILITY", "   5.1 Barrier-free access must be maintained to all floors in public use during", "       the works, unless the Fund agrees otherwise in writing."]}];
