const sourceDocs=[{"id": "Project_brief_p3", "lines": ["From: Daniel Koh, Director, Estate Development, Harbourline Town Council Subject:", "      Harbourline Community Hub Refurbishment — project brief", "", "      Background. Harbourline Community Hub is a four-storey building completed in", "      1994, about 9,800 m² gross floor area. It houses a sports hall, multi-purpose rooms, a", "      tuition centre and a small food court, all on leases or licences. Usage has fallen, the", "      M&E plant is at end of life, and residents have asked for childcare and senior services", "      closer to home.", "", "      Objectives. Refurbish the Hub into an integrated community facility that serves", "      residents of all ages, improves accessibility and energy performance, and becomes", "      the estate's flagship shared space.", "", "      Scope. The refurbished Hub will include:", "", "           an upgraded multi-purpose sports hall", "           a new early childhood centre for about 100 children, run by our selected operator,", "           Little Harbour Learning", "           an active ageing centre, operator to be appointed", "           a community kitchen and food court refresh", "           a rooftop community garden", "           full barrier-free access, new lifts and replacement of M&E systems", "", "      Budget and time. Approved budget is S$18.5 million. Sixty per cent is funded by a", "      central grant released in tranches against milestones; grant conditions will follow.", "      Works are to complete within 22 months, with the Hub fully open by the fourth", "      quarter of 2028.", "", "      Delivery. We intend a single design-and-build contract. The Hub must remain open to", "      residents throughout the works. Residents will be consulted on the design. Little", "      Harbour Learning wishes to begin enrolment in month 18.", "", "      Reporting. The Estate Development Committee meets weekly and expects a short", "      status update. The grant body requires a monthly progress report. Our current", "      tracking is in spreadsheets.", "", "      Success. A fully operational Hub, delivered on budget, with high resident", "      satisfaction.", "", "", "", "", "                                                                                             Page 3 of 11", "", "MA6094 Capstone Brief — Harbourline Community Hub", "", "", "", "", "  "]}, {"id": "Sponsor_Answers_Round1", "lines": ["Capstone Sponsor Answers — Round 1", "", "", "", "", "  Capstone Sponsor Answers — Round 1", "    Oct 23, 2026        · ​@Spurthi", "", "  Harbourline Community Hub Refurbishment. Answers from Daniel Koh, Director, Estate", "  Development, Harbourline Town Council (played by the instructor). Questions came from", "  one team; answers apply to every team.", "", "", "  Q1. Does the 22-month timeline include tendering the design-and-", "  build contract?", "  No. The 22 months is construction only, counted from site possession.", "", "       The design-and-build contract was awarded on 18 December 2026.", "       Site possession is Monday 4 January 2027. Plan from that date.", "       Tendering is not on your critical path. Design is, because the contractor designs and", "       builds under the same contract.", "", "", "  Q2. Who appoints the active ageing centre operator, and when?", "  The Town Council appoints the operator through its own procurement, separate from the", "  construction contract.", "", "       An expression of interest will be issued in February 2027.", "       Council procurement policy requires at least three responses before an appointment.", "       There is no confirmed appointment date. Schedule and track it as a dependency.", "       Check the grant conditions (data pack file 07) for anything that depends on this", "       appointment.", "", "", "  Q3. How can M&E be replaced if the Hub stays open, and what", "  closes first?", "  The Council's position is that the Hub remains open to residents throughout the works.", "", "       The contractor is responsible for the phasing plan. No closures have been agreed yet.", "       The Council will consider short, well-notified closures of individual areas if they are", "       shown to be necessary.", "", "", "", "", "                                                                                             Page 1 of 2", "", "Capstone Sponsor Answers — Round 1", "", "", "", "", "       Whatever is closed, residents must keep barrier-free access to every floor in public", "       use.", "", "  The early childhood centre and active ageing centre are new facilities and do not exist yet,", "  so they cannot close. The areas in use today are the sports hall, multi-purpose rooms,", "  tuition centre and food court. The Council has not set a closure priority among them. If", "  your plan needs one, state it as an assumption, show the impact of each option, and bring", "  it to the sponsor as a decision.", "", "", "  Q4. Does resident consultation happen before tender or during", "  design and build?", "  During design and build, because tendering is complete.", "", "       The Council's Community Engagement team runs it, not the contractor.", "       It runs 1 to 28 February 2027: online, paper forms at the Hub, and one town hall.", "       The results go to the contractor as design input.", "", "  Treat consultation as a Council work package whose summary feeds the contractor's", "  design stage.", "", "", "  Q5. Who funds the remaining 40%?", "  The Town Council funds the balance from its own capital reserves.", "", "       No other grant is being sought, so no fundraising work package is needed.", "       The monthly report is a progress report to the grant body, not a funding request.", "       Read the grant conditions (data pack file 07) carefully. The 60% applies to eligible cost,", "       and what counts as eligible may change your funding picture.", "", "  Any question the sponsor has not answered stays an open assumption in your register.", "  Follow-up questions go through the CP2 round.", "", "", "", "", "                                                                                            Page 2 of 2", ""]}, {"id": "00_README.txt", "lines": ["HARBOURLINE COMMUNITY HUB REFURBISHMENT — CAPSTONE DATA PACK", "MA6094 Agentic AI for Project Management", "", "Everything in this pack is FICTIONAL. Harbourline Town Council, Kestrel Harbour", "Builders, Little Harbour Learning, the Neighbourhood Renewal Fund and every person", "named are invented for teaching. Do not add real data to any file or prompt.", "", "The pack covers the project's first three months: January to March 2027.", "Contract works started on Monday 4 January 2027.", "", "FILES", "  01_EDC_minutes_Jan-Mar2027.txt          Estate Development Committee, 6 meetings", "  02_Contractor_progress_report_Jan2027.pdf", "  02_Contractor_progress_report_Feb2027.pdf", "  02_Contractor_progress_report_Mar2027.pdf", "  03_Contract_deliverables_schedule.csv", "  04_Seed_risk_register.csv                inherited from the 2025 feasibility study", "  05_Resident_consultation_responses.csv   consultation run 1-28 Feb 2027", "  06_Lessons_learned_Seabreeze_Hub.txt     an earlier hub refurbishment, 2019-2021", "  07_Grant_milestone_tranche_schedule.txt  Neighbourhood Renewal Fund conditions", "", "HOW TO USE IT", "  - Together with the project brief and posted sponsor answers, this pack is the", "    ONLY source your memory, risk and reporting modules may draw on.", "  - The files were written by different people at different times. They do not", "    always agree with each other or with the brief. When they conflict, your system", "    should say so and cite both sources, not silently pick one.", "  - Cite file name and meeting, page, row ID or section when your system uses a fact.", "  - CSV files are UTF-8. Some consultation comments are in Chinese, Malay or Tamil."]}, {"id": "01_EDC_minutes_Jan-Mar2027.txt", "lines": ["HARBOURLINE TOWN COUNCIL", "ESTATE DEVELOPMENT COMMITTEE (EDC) — MINUTES, HARBOURLINE COMMUNITY HUB REFURBISHMENT", "Extract: six meetings, January to March 2027", "", "Standing attendees: Daniel Koh (Director, Estate Development, Chair), Mei Ling Ong", "(Finance Manager), Ravi Shankar (Project Manager, Council), Farah Aziz (Community", "Engagement Lead), Kestrel Harbour Builders (KHB) represented by Jonathan Lim (Project", "Director). Others as listed.", "", "======================================================================", "MEETING 1 — Thursday 7 January 2027", "======================================================================", "1.1 Contract award. The design-and-build contract was awarded to Kestrel Harbour", "    Builders Pte Ltd on 18 December 2026 at a contract sum of S$16.42 million.", "    Site possession given Monday 4 January 2027. Consultancy and authority fees are", "    estimated at S$0.90 million, held outside the contract.", "1.2 Ms Ong noted the approved budget of S$18.5 million leaves about S$1.18 million", "    once fees are deducted, and asked whether this is to be treated as contingency.", "    No decision recorded.", "1.3 The Chair reaffirmed the Council's commitment that the Hub REMAINS OPEN to", "    residents throughout the works. KHB to submit a phasing plan by 1 February.", "1.4 Grant conditions from the Neighbourhood Renewal Fund (NRF) not yet received.", "    ACTION: D. Koh to obtain by 15 January.", "1.5 Active ageing centre operator: expression of interest (EOI) to be issued in", "    February. ACTION: R. Shankar.", "1.6 The EDC will meet weekly on Thursdays for the duration of the works.", "", "======================================================================", "MEETING 2 — Thursday 21 January 2027", "======================================================================", "Additional attendee: Grace Teo (Little Harbour Learning, Centre Development Manager)", "2.1 NRF grant conditions received 19 January (see file 07). Ms Ong reported that the", "    Fund caps ELIGIBLE cost at S$17.0 million and the 60% grant applies to eligible", "    cost only. The food court refresh and rooftop community garden are listed as", "    ineligible. Ms Ong to report the funding effect at the next meeting.", "2.2 Ms Teo confirmed Little Harbour Learning intends to open enrolment in July 2028", "    and admit the first children in January 2029. She asked for handover of the", "    childcare floor \"by month 18\" to complete fit-out and licensing.", "2.3 To reduce load on members, the EDC will meet FORTNIGHTLY from February. Written", "    updates may be circulated in alternate weeks.", "2.4 KHB reported mobilisation complete; site office established in the car park.", "2.5 Meeting 1 action 1.4 closed.", "", "======================================================================", "MEETING 3 — Thursday 4 February 2027", "======================================================================", "3.1 KHB phasing plan received. KHB advised that:", "    (a) replacing the two lifts in the east core requires closing the east core for", "        about 14 weeks, during which levels 3 and 4 have no barrier-free access;", "    (b) the sports hall roof and M&E replacement needs the hall closed for about", "        10 weeks;", "    (c) the food court must close for 6 weeks for kitchen exhaust and grease-trap works.", "3.2 The Chair stated the Hub must remain open and asked KHB to \"resequence where", "    possible\". Mr Lim said a temporary lift is possible but not priced. No decision.", "3.3 Resident consultation launched online on 1 February, closing 28 February. Paper", "    forms available at the Hub counter. One town hall to be held on 13 February.", "3.4 Active ageing operator EOI issued 2 February, closing 26 February.", "3.5 Ms Ong reported the funding effect of item 2.1 (figures in her paper, not minuted).", "", "======================================================================", "MEETING 4 — Thursday 25 February 2027", "======================================================================", "4.1 KHB baseline programme submitted. Key dates: practical completion", "    31 December 2028; childcare floor handover to operator for fit-out", "    month 20 (August 2028); phased reopening of sports hall from month 14.", "4.2 The Chair queried how a 31 December 2028 completion fits the \"fully open by", "    Q4 2028\" commitment. Mr Shankar to reconcile and report.", "4.3 Ms Teo (by email, read out) noted an August 2028 handover does not allow the", "    licensing period her organisation needs before a January 2029 intake.", "4.4 Active ageing operator EOI: one response received. Council procurement policy", "    requires at least three. EOI extended to 30 April 2027.", "4.5 Town hall on 13 February attended by about 40 residents.", "", "======================================================================", "MEETING 5 — Thursday 11 March 2027", "======================================================================", "5.1 KHB reported suspected asbestos-containing ceiling boards on level 2 (west wing)", "    during soft-strip. Works in that zone stopped on 3 March. Specialist survey", "    commissioned; KHB estimates removal at S$0.35–0.60 million and 4–6 weeks.", "    The 2025 feasibility study had stated no hazardous materials were expected.", "5.2 Structural engineer's note: the roof slab needs strengthening before it can carry", "    the rooftop garden soil load. Cost not yet estimated.", "5.3 Resident consultation closed 28 February with 214 responses recorded.", "    Ms Aziz to present a summary at Meeting 6.", "5.4 Mr Shankar has not yet reconciled the programme (action 4.2). Carried forward.", "", "======================================================================", "MEETING 6 — Thursday 25 March 2027", "======================================================================", "6.1 NRF Tranche 1 claim submitted 19 March.", "6.2 Ms Ong drew attention t